  "output": "Now I have enough. Here's the full analysis based on the actual code, not speculation.\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: ConvertPro\n\n### 1. N+1 Queries\n\n**`ConversionsController#index` — unbounded + no blob eager loading**\n\n`app/controllers/conversions_controller.rb:5`\n```ruby\n# BAD — fetches ALL conversions, then the view fires N blob queries\n@conversions = current_user.conversions.order(created_at: :desc)\n\n# FIX\n@conversions = current_user.conversions\n                            .includes(output_file_attachment: :blob)\n                            .order(created_at: :desc)\n                            .limit(50)\n```\n\nEvery `conversion.output_file.blob.filename` in the view (filename display, download links) fires a separate `SELECT * FROM active_storage_blobs WHERE id = ?`. With 50 conversions that's 50 extra queries.\n\n---\n\n**`ConversionsController#show` + `#status` — duplicate blob load via ToolRecommender**\n\n`app/controllers/conversions_controller.rb:27-28` and `38-39`\n\n`ToolRecommender.for` calls `conversion.output_file.blob.content_type` (`tool_recommender.rb:27`). The blob is already loaded by the controller action (if you fix #1 above for the single-record path), but it isn't preloaded here — ActiveStorage will re-query on every `.blob` access unless the association is eager-loaded:\n\n```ruby\n# In authorized_conversion, after find_by:\nConversion.includes(output_file_attachment: :blob).find_by(id: id)\n```\n\nThis hits on **every status poll** (every 2.5 s during processing).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Missing Database Indexes\n\n`db/schema.rb` — `conversions` table has indexes only on `user_id` and `client_operation_id`.\n\n```ruby\n# Missing — add via migration:\n\nadd_index :conversions, :status\n# CleanupJob queries by status (pending/completed); currently a full table scan\n\nadd_index :conversions, :created_at\n# ConversionsController#index ORDER BY created_at DESC uses no index\n\nadd_index :analytics_events, :tool_id\n# Any analytics query filtering or grouping by tool_id is a full table scan\n```\n\nGenerate with:\n```bash\nrails g migration AddMissingIndexes\n```\n```ruby\ndef change\n  add_index :conversions, :status\n  add_index :conversions, :created_at\n  add_index :analytics_events, :tool_id\nend\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Synchronous Analytics Writes on Every Request\n\n`app/services/analytics.rb:34`\n\n```ruby\n# BAD — synchronous DB INSERT in the request cycle\nAnalyticsEvent.create!(...)\n\n# FIX — fire-and-forget; Rails 7.1+ async adapter makes this one-line\nAnalyticsEvent.create_later(...)   # if using async adapter\n\n# or wrap in after_action / perform_later pattern:\nAnalyticsEventJob.perform_later(name, user_id:, tool_id:, properties:)\n```\n\n`tools_controller.rb#show` fires 1 sync write on every page view. `conversions_controller.rb#download` fires 2. These add DB write round-trips directly to response time.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Redundant ToolRegistry Linear Scans\n\n`app/services/tool_recommender.rb:16-21` + `app/controllers/conversions_controller.rb:27,38`\n\n`ToolRegistry.tools.find { |t| t[:class_name] == ... }` is O(n) over ~30 tools, called 3+ times per show/status request. Status is polled every 2.5 s.\n\n```ruby\n# app/services/tool_registry.rb — add after self.tools = [...]\nself.tools_by_class = tools.index_by { |t| t[:class_name] }\nself.tools_by_id    = tools.index_by { |t| t[:id] }\n\ndef self.find(id) = tools_by_id[id]\ndef self.find_by_class(class_name) = tools_by_class[class_name]\n```\n\nThen replace all `.find { |t| t[:class_name] == ... }` and `.find { |t| t[:id] == ... }` calls with `ToolRegistry.find_by_class(name)` / `ToolRegistry.find(id)`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Fixed Polling Interval — No Backoff\n\n`app/javascript/controllers/poll_controller.js:29-31`\n\n```js\n// BAD — polls every 2.5s for a 60-second OCR job = 24 wasted requests\nschedule() {\n  this.timer = setTimeout(() => this.poll(), this.intervalValue)\n}\n\n// FIX — exponential backoff, cap at 15s\nschedule() {\n  this._delay = Math.min((this._delay || this.intervalValue) * 1.5, 15000)\n  this.timer = setTimeout(() => this.poll(), this._delay)\n}\n\nconnect() {\n  this._delay = this.intervalValue  // reset on fresh connect\n  // ... rest unchanged\n}\n```\n\nA 30-second job currently fires ~12 polls. With backoff: ~6. No behavior change — the server still terminates polling when `active` is false.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Unnecessary `user.reload` in ConversionLimiter\n\n`app/services/conversion_limiter.rb:44-45` and `56-57`\n\n```ruby\n# BAD — extra SELECT after an atomic UPDATE we already know succeeded\nrows = User.where(...).update_all(\"conversions_count = conversions_count + 1\")\nclaimed = rows == 1\n@user.reload if claimed  # ← round-trip to DB\n\n# FIX — update in-memory attribute directly\nif claimed\n  @user.conversions_count += 1\n  @user.clear_attribute_changes([:conversions_count])\nend\n```\n\nSame fix in `refund!`. Eliminates one `SELECT users WHERE id = ?` per conversion claim/refund.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Sequential Cloudinary HTTP Calls on Download\n\n`app/controllers/conversions_controller.rb:192-210`\n\n```ruby\n# BAD — two blocking Cloudinary API calls in the worst case\n[\"raw\", \"image\"].each do |resource_type|\n  Cloudinary::Api.resource(key, resource_type: resource_type)  # HTTP call\n  ...\nend\n```\n\n**Option A** — store `resource_type` on the blob's metadata at upload time (in the tool that creates the output), so the download path always knows which type to use without probing.\n\n**Option B** — cache the result in Rails.cache keyed by blob key:\n```ruby\nresource_type = Rails.cache.fetch(\"cloudinary_type:#{key}\", expires_in: 1.hour) do\n  [\"raw\", \"image\"].each { |rt| ... probe and return rt ... }\nend\n```\n\nRepeated downloads of the same file stop hitting Cloudinary's API entirely.\n\n---\n\n### 8. No Memory Leaks Found\n\n`poll_controller.js:25-26` correctly calls `clearTimeout(this.timer)` on `disconnect()`. Stimulus's lifecycle handles the rest. No JS memory leaks.\n\n---\n\n## Priority Order\n\n| # | Issue | Impact | Effort |\n|---|-------|--------|--------|\n| 1 | Missing indexes (`status`, `created_at`, `tool_id`) | High — full table scans at scale | 10 min migration |\n| 2 | No blob eager loading on conversions index | High — N+1 on every history page | 1 line |\n| 3 | Async analytics writes | Medium — adds latency to every tracked action | 1 job class |\n| 4 | ToolRegistry hash lookups | Low-medium — per-poll overhead | 15 min refactor |\n| 5 | Polling backoff | Medium — wasted requests on slow jobs | 5 lines |\n| 6 | ConversionLimiter reload | Low | 2 lines |\n| 7 | Cloudinary caching | Low-medium — only hits on download | 10 lines |\n\nItems 1 and 2 are the highest value — zero-cost query reduction for existing users. Start there.\n",
